div.p:
“The Shenandoah is a vessel of 1,100 tons and 250 horse-power, with four 8-inch
                    smooth-bore guns, two 32-pound rifles and two 12-pounders, also smooth. She was
                    the Sea King, belonging to the London, Bombay and
                    Calcutta Steam Navigation Company; built by Stevens and Sons, Glasgow, in 1863;
                    steams 11 miles an hour; carries 43 men and two officers, most of them English;
                    cleared from London for Bombay in September, 1863.
